  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An elevator (lift) and its load accelerate vertically upwards.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Which statement is correct in this situation?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">The net force on the load is zero.</li><li data-label=\"B\">The tension in the cable is equal but opposite to the combined weight of the elevator and its load.</li><li data-label=\"C\">The normal reaction force on the load is equal but opposite to the force on the elevator from the load.</li><li data-label=\"D\">The elevator and its load are in translational equilibrium.</li></ol>"
  },
